      "@type": "kto:EndgameType",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Philidor position",
      "skos:definition": "The basic drawing method in rook and pawn against rook: with the defending king on the queening square, the defending rook holds its third rank to keep the attacking king out, and once the pawn advances it drops to the far end of the board to check from behind.",
