      "@id": "kt:blockade",
      "@type": "kto:StrategicConcept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Blockade",
      "skos:definition": "The strategy of stopping an enemy pawn, above all a passed or isolated pawn, by planting a piece on the square directly in front of it; systematised by Aron Nimzowitsch, who held that a pawn should be physically blocked rather than merely watched.",
