      "skos:prefLabel": "Forsyth–Edwards Notation",
      "skos:definition": "A one-line text format that records a complete chess position in six space-separated fields (piece placement, side to move, castling rights, en passant target, halfmove clock and move number); it extends David Forsyth's 1883 position notation and was standardised by Steven J. Edwards in the 1994 PGN specification.",
