      "@type": "kto:Rule",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Stalemate",
      "skos:definition": "The rule that a game is drawn when the player to move has no legal move and their king is not in check; once a win or a loss depending on time and place, it has been a draw everywhere since the mid-nineteenth century.",
