    {
      "@id": "kt:adriaan-de-groot",
      "@type": "kto:Person",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Adriaan de Groot",
      "skos:definition": "Dutch psychologist and chess master (1914–2006) who represented the Netherlands at two Chess Olympiads and whose 1946 thesis, translated as Thought and Choice in Chess, founded the experimental study of how chess players think, search and remember positions.",
